               <head>Qurʾān, in three parts</head>
               <msContents>
                  <summary>A Qurʾān in Maghribī script, now kept in the collection as three parts:
                     the Qurʾān 71(loose leaves, out of order); Sūrat Yā Sīn (4 leaves, more worn and
                     folded); and a single leaf with poetry and the colophon. The same hand and leaf
                     size suggest they were once a single manuscript, with the colophon leaf
                     probably at the end.</summary>
                  <msItem xml:id="UOL_MS_284-item1">
                     <title xml:lang="ar-Latn-x-lc" key="work_112">Qurʾān</title>
                     <title xml:lang="ar" key="work_112">قرآن</title>
                     <title xml:lang="ar-Latn-x-lc" key="work_23685">Sūrat Yā Sīn</title>
                     <title xml:lang="ar" key="work_23685">سورة يس</title>
                     <colophon>On the poetry leaf, in a cloud-shaped frame: <quote xml:lang="ar">كمل
                           الكتاب … والصلاة والسلام على رسول الله … كاتبه</quote>
                        <persName role="scr" key="" cert="medium">Bīrān Muḥammad ibn
                           Muḥammad</persName>. Undated.</colophon>
                     <note>
                        <p>Verses separated by red circles.</p>
                     </note>
                     <textLang mainLang="ar">Arabic</textLang>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
